  \p{Ann Arbor, MI}
  \p{EECS 4107}
  \<html:a>[href]{mailto:kellenkk@umich.edu}{kellenkk@umich.edu}}
}

\p{I am a PhD student at the [[umich]] as part of the [Electrical and Computer Engineering program](https://ece.engin.umich.edu/), where my work #{\in} {programming languages} #{\cap} {computer architecture} #{\cap} {LLMs} #{\cap} {reinforcement learning}. I am advised by Prof. [[xinyuwang]] and Prof. [[satishnarayanasamy]].
Currently, \mark{I am interested in automated kernel generation across accelerators. In particular, neurosymbolic approaches to preserve guarantees and limit costs}. With this, I am looking into {[kernel DSLs](5PSC), [[IR7B]], [formal synthesis](Q30B), LLM "[vibe compilers](AV36)"}. I am also recreationally interested in Unix (see my [dotfiles](https://github.com/kkanarios32/dotfiles)) and in a past life I did research in [reinforcement learning algorithms](bib). 
}

\p{Previously, I obtained a BS from the [[umich]] in Mathematics and Computer Science, where I graduated with honors and high honors respectively. I also obtained my MS in Electrical and Computer Engineering from [[umich]]. During both my undergrad and masters, I worked with [[leiying]] as part of the [SURE Program](https://sure.engin.umich.edu/), a TA for [EECS 602](https://sites.google.com/view/intro-to-rl/home), a GSRA, and a GSI for [ECE 567](https://bulletin.engin.umich.edu/courses/eecs/). My full resume is available \<html:a>[style]{text-decoration: underline;}[href]{\route-asset{assets/files/kellen-kanarios-resume.pdf}}{here}.
}

\p{
  If you are a student at [[umich]] and are interested in research, I am advising a few undergraduates. For potential projects, see my [[Z902]]. If you want to take one on, [schedule a meeting](https://calendly.com/kellenkk-umich/30min)!
}

